From 5735e16b7b1c23360e3c7749528a2f63997e795b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rustcc-build <rustcc@localhost>
Date: Sat, 9 May 2026 17:00:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] P09.46-B1-hir-def: ClassId / AdtId::ClassId /
 VariantId::ClassId stubs

Pure data-structure scaffolding for rustcc Phase 2 Option B.

Adds:
- ClassLoc, ClassId, intern_class / lookup_intern_class (parallel
  to StructId in hir-def/src/lib.rs)
- AdtId::ClassId(ClassId) variant with impl_from! routing to
  AdtId, GenericDefId, ModuleDefId, AttrDefId
- VariantId::ClassId(ClassId) variant
- ErasedFileAstIdKind::Class + register_has_name_ast_id! entry
  in span/src/ast_id.rs
- intern_class on InternDatabase trait

Each non-exhaustive match-Adt site in hir-def gets either:
- A 'treat-like-struct' Class arm where the struct path makes
  semantic sense (resolver attrs, attr collection, builtin
  derive sourcing, item-scope kind classification, hir-display)
- An 'unimplemented' stub where ClassSignature would need to
  be wired (generics::Generics::with_store / with_source_map,
  expr_store::ExpressionStore::of for Signature owner,
  signatures::VariantFields::with_source_map, src::child_source
  for VariantId, expr_store/pretty for VariantId+AdtId headers).
  These stubs are unreachable at runtime: lowering doesn't
  produce ClassIds yet, so no caller can construct a value
  that hits these match arms. B.2 wires real ClassSignature
  lowering and replaces the stubs.

Verification:
- cargo check -p hir-def: 0 errors (was 25 after AdtId variant
  was added)
- cargo test -p parser: 315 passed, 0 failed (Phase 1 baseline)
- cargo test -p syntax: 51 passed, 0 failed (Phase 1 baseline)

Remaining workspace errors after this commit (~42 in hir-ty +
hir + ide-*) are addressed in subsequent commits in this series.
